BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Festival (formerly Halloween in the Hills)\, Brown County Sta
 te Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261017T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261017T210000
UID:06c24a1c67cee0f86d781073bdffe5c2@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:Brown County State Park celebrates Halloween on October 17th t
 his year! Contests: 4pm: The Pumpkin Carving Contest: Have your carved pum
 pkin at the Nature Center picnic shelter before 4pm to be considered! Pump
 kins will be judged in three age categories: 10 and under\, 11-17\, and 18
  or older. Pumpkins will be displayed from 7pm to 9pm at the Friends&#39\;
  Circle.&nbsp\; The top contestant in each category wins a 2026 Indiana St
 ate Park Entrance Pass\; 2nd and 3rd place get a swag bag. 5pm: Campsite D
 ecorating Contest: Have your campsite decorated for Halloween. Register at
  the campground gatehouse by 5pm. Please get a copy of and follow all rule
 s given at the campground gatehouse (no nails in trees\, no digging\, etc)
 .&nbsp\; Have your campsite ready by 7pm at the latest for judging. The to
 p three campsites win vouchers for camping at Brown County State Park. Fir
 st place gets 5 nights\, second gets 3\, and third gets 1. Programs: 12pm 
 to 4pm: Halloween Arts and Crafts: Stop by the Nature Center in the aftern
 oon to do some crafts\, including animal Halloween masks! You may stay and
  use our supplies or take paper to go. 5:30pm to 7pm: Trick or Treating in
  the campground. Visit marked participating sites to trick or treat! Parti
 cipating sites can pick up a sign from the campground gatehouse.&nbsp\; Pl
 ease stay on foot and do not trick or treat out of cars.&nbsp\; 7pm to 9pm
 : Campfire Stories: Bring a story to read or a tale to tell. Save any scar
 y stories for after 8:30pm. Feel free to bring campfire snacks! The Pumpki
 n Carving Contest entrees will be on display. Hikes: 7pm to 9pm: Candlelig
 ht Hike: Hike the Discovery Trail at the Nature Center. The path will be l
 it by small candles\, but your own flashlight is advised as a backup! Wear
  close-toed shoes or boots\, do not wear sandals or flip flops.
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/BrownCountySP
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
